Dependencies
------------

- github.com/beevik/etree (BSD-2-Clause, Copyright Brett Vickers):
  XML element trees for signing and verification.
- github.com/russellhaering/goxmldsig (Apache-2.0, Copyright Russell
  Haering and contributors): enveloped XML signatures.
- github.com/jonboulle/clockwork (Apache-2.0), through goxmldsig.
- golang.org/x/crypto (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors): OCSP
  requests and responses.
- github.com/cB-Sigma/xsd (Apache-2.0, Copyright Abhinav Gautam): the XSD
  engine of package capxsd.
- The Go standard library (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright The Go Authors).

The test-only module interop/ also uses github.com/tannerryan/cap
(BSD-2-Clause, Copyright Tanner Ryan) to cross-check this one, and reads
the sample alerts it ships from the Go module cache; it is not a
dependency of this module. With SIGMA_CAP_INTEROP=1 it also builds
Docker images of xmlschema (MIT, https://github.com/sissaschool/xmlschema)
and xmlsec1 (the XML Security Library, MIT, from Alpine packages) to check
schemas and signatures; they are fetched at build time, not redistributed.

Test data
---------

Every alert, sender, identifier, area, key and certificate in the tests
and the examples is made up or generated at run time.
